  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certifies that on 6th March 2006, the erection of a single storey rear and side infill extension with dimensions 3.6 metres wide, 4.9 and 1.1 metres deep, and on average 2.65 metres high, returning a volume of 27.0 cu. m, as shown on drawing numbers MS01.11 and 12, received 06th March 2006, was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nFollowing the proposed extensions consisting of a single storey side and rear extension, the resulting building would fall within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1,Class A and Class C, of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995.\r\n"
